[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3709855949","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113107#issuecomment-3709855949","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113107","id":3709855949,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dH-jN","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T10:31:50Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T10:31:50Z","body":"I squashed the commits, amended the commit message for clarity, and fixed the remaining style issue.\r\n\r\nThe fix seems valid, though I wonder if it needs to do as much. Camera3DPreview is constructed with its child `sub_viewport`, so it seems expected that `sub_viewport` is valid until Camera3DPreview is destructed. But the problem is that the signal pattern bypasses that and we get sort of a race condition between handling the `settings_changed` signal and destructing the preview (I assume).\r\n\r\nThe simplest fix would just be\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/editor/scene/3d/camera_3d_editor_plugin.cpp b/editor/scene/3d/camera_3d_editor_plugin.cpp\r\nindex 4dc3cdfec2..f81c9c5ef1 100644\r\n--- a/editor/scene/3d/camera_3d_editor_plugin.cpp\r\n+++ b/editor/scene/3d/camera_3d_editor_plugin.cpp\r\n@@ -80,6 +80,9 @@ Camera3DEditor::Camera3DEditor() {\r\n }\r\n \r\n void Camera3DPreview::_update_sub_viewport_size() {\r\n+\tif (!sub_viewport) {\r\n+\t\treturn;\r\n+\t}\r\n \tsub_viewport->set_size(Node3DEditor::get_camera_viewport_size(camera));\r\n }\r\n \r\n```\r\n\r\nOr alternatively, just disconnecting the signal in `NOTIFICATION_EXIT_TREE`.\r\n\r\nBut the approach in this PR should also solve the issue, while just doing a bit more manual memory management than should otherwise be necessary with a parent-owned node.\r\n\r\nWDYT @KoBeWi @YeldhamDev?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3709855949/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3709883924","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113107#issuecomment-3709883924","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113107","id":3709883924,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dIFYU","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T10:40:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T10:40:33Z","body":"What are the exact reproduction steps for the crash? Like\r\n\r\n> and you have a Camera3D preview showing, but the underlying Camera is removed\r\n\r\nwhen does this happen?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3709883924/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3709918818","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113107#issuecomment-3709918818","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113107","id":3709918818,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dIN5i","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T10:50:17Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T10:50:17Z","body":"Probably unknown as this is based on telemetry crash reports for Xogot (Godot iOS editor fork).\r\nSo Miguel probably based this explanation off reading the code and the stacktrace.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3709918818/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3709968843","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113107#issuecomment-3709968843","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113107","id":3709968843,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dIaHL","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T11:04:58Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T11:06:34Z","body":"It's a child of Camera3DPreview, so it gets freed when Camera3DPreview gets freed, which I assume happens when stopping the preview/removing a camera. If this happens at the same time where `settings_changed` is emitted, I think a race condition can still happen where the callback gets called even though the Camera3DPreview is mid-destruction, can't it?\r\n\r\n> It's never re-assigned either, so if it does get freed for whatever reason, `if (!sub_viewport)` is checking invalid pointer.\r\n\r\nRight, so my \"minimal\" fix is a bit too minimal, resetting the pointer to `nullptr` in `NOTIFICATION_EXIT_TREE` might be needed too (or as Miguel did it on `tree_exiting`). I'm just not sure we need to go all the way and queue free `sub_viewport` just before it gets freed anyway.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3709968843/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3710389038","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113107#issuecomment-3710389038","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113107","id":3710389038,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dKAsu","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T13:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T13:18:38Z","body":"So this could connect to viewport's `tree_exited` and then set the pointer to null.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3710389038/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3804341226","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113107#issuecomment-3804341226","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113107","id":3804341226,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iwaPq","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T10:24:06Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T10:24:06Z","body":"#115436 may be related (2D editor crash on Android).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3804341226/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]